1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,441
Mummy placed her wedding bangles on the jeweller's counter.

2
00:00:07,441 --> 00:00:14,205
She thought, how expensive gold must have become in all these years.

3
00:00:14,205 --> 00:00:21,646
Today I'll get a good amount. The jeweller weighed the bangles, ran the calculator,

4
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:28,410
and said the amount with a smile. Mummy's face fell.

5
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:32,510
The amount wasn't small, but it was far less than she expected.

6
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:36,610
The jeweller said, madam, you don't get the money for the design back.

7
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:40,710
I only weigh the gold, and that too after checking its purity.

8
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:41,530
Mummy said,

9
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:45,630
when we bought it, we paid in full for the design too.

10
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:46,860
The jeweller stayed quiet.

11
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:50,890
At home, Mummy told Papa everything. Papa said,

12
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:54,517
gold never cheats you, it's safe.

13
00:00:54,517 --> 00:00:58,145
My sister looked up from her phone and asked, Papa,

14
00:00:58,145 --> 00:01:01,369
are safe and earning the same thing?

15
00:01:01,369 --> 00:01:04,190
Silence fell over the room for a while.

16
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:09,348
This story belongs to almost every Indian home.

17
00:01:09,348 --> 00:01:15,796
We see gold as security, and rightly so,

18
00:01:15,796 --> 00:01:19,665
it helps in hard times.

19
00:01:19,665 --> 00:01:28,047
But the real question is which gold actually earns.

20
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:32,560
Jewellery, gold ETF, or sovereign gold bond?

21
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,219
Today's questions are simple. First,

22
00:01:35,219 --> 00:01:39,208
where does the making charge on jewellery go? Second,

23
00:01:39,208 --> 00:01:42,310
who counts the locker cost? Third,

24
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:46,298
how do you get an extra 2.5 percent on a gold bond?

25
00:01:46,298 --> 00:01:50,730
And finally, when is jewellery a purchase, and when is it an investment.

26
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:55,603
Let's go back to the day the bangles were bought.

27
00:01:55,603 --> 00:01:59,147
The wedding preparations were on, the house was full of joy.

28
00:01:59,147 --> 00:02:03,135
Papa and Mummy were sitting in the jeweller's shop.

29
00:02:03,135 --> 00:02:06,679
In front of them, trays of shining bangles, necklaces and earrings.

30
00:02:06,679 --> 00:02:09,780
Every item had a price tag.

31
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:13,854
The jeweller made the bill, and it had many lines. First,

32
00:02:13,854 --> 00:02:18,336
the weight of the gold and that day's rate. Second, the making charge.

33
00:02:18,336 --> 00:02:22,818
Then GST on top. Papa only looked at the total written at the bottom,

34
00:02:22,818 --> 00:02:25,670
and paid without asking any questions.

35
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:30,189
Making charge means the labour for making the jewellery,

36
00:02:30,189 --> 00:02:35,999
the money for the craftsman's work. Gold is gold,

37
00:02:35,999 --> 00:02:40,518
but the engraving on the bangles, the latticework of the necklace,

38
00:02:40,518 --> 00:02:46,328
all this is handwork. The finer the design,

39
00:02:46,328 --> 00:02:52,783
the higher the making charge. And this money didn't go into the gold,

40
00:02:52,783 --> 00:02:54,720
it went into the design.

41
00:02:54,720 --> 00:03:00,038
Now here comes the part nobody tells you.

42
00:03:00,038 --> 00:03:03,228
When you go to sell your jewellery,

43
00:03:03,228 --> 00:03:06,951
the jeweller only looks at the weight of the gold.

44
00:03:06,951 --> 00:03:10,673
The money you paid as making charges does not come back.

45
00:03:10,673 --> 00:03:16,523
On top of that, there may be some deduction on old jewellery too,

46
00:03:16,523 --> 00:03:18,650
in the name of purity.

47
00:03:18,650 --> 00:03:23,379
Understand what this means. The day you bought the jewellery,

48
00:03:23,379 --> 00:03:30,135
some of your money was gone forever that very day.

49
00:03:30,135 --> 00:03:36,891
Only when the gold price rises will that loss first be made up.

50
00:03:36,891 --> 00:03:41,620
Only after that will the real earning begin.

51
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:47,700
So the jewellery race starts from behind.

52
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:50,150
It's the same story with GST.

53
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:54,643
When buying, you paid GST on both the gold and the making charges.

54
00:03:54,643 --> 00:03:58,319
When selling, the jeweller does not give that GST back to you.

55
00:03:58,319 --> 00:04:02,403
That is also a plain expense. It looks small on the bill,

56
00:04:02,403 --> 00:04:05,670
but years later it looks big in the accounts.

57
00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:09,214
So is buying jewellery wrong? Not at all.

58
00:04:09,214 --> 00:04:14,086
The shine of Mummy's bangle at your daughter's wedding,

59
00:04:14,086 --> 00:04:18,959
its value can't be worked out on a calculator. It's happiness, it's memories,

60
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:23,388
it's tradition. Just don't call it an investment. It's a purchase,

61
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:25,160
like a new saree.

62
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:27,117
Now the second question.

63
00:04:27,117 --> 00:04:34,945
After the wedding, Papa didn't feel right keeping the jewellery at home.

64
00:04:34,945 --> 00:04:40,816
He feared theft, and guests kept coming and going.

65
00:04:40,816 --> 00:04:47,339
So Papa went to the bank and asked the Bank Uncle for a locker.

66
00:04:47,339 --> 00:04:53,210
Bank Uncle gave him a form and told him the yearly rent.

67
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:59,905
At an SBI branch in a big city, the rent for a small locker is about 2,000 rupees a year.

68
00:04:59,905 --> 00:05:04,089
And even that 2,000 is not the full amount, GST is extra on top.

69
00:05:04,089 --> 00:05:07,436
Papa said, just this much? Okay, fine.

70
00:05:07,436 --> 00:05:11,620
And that rent started getting quietly deducted from the account every year.

71
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,396
18 percent GST is charged on the locker,

72
00:05:14,396 --> 00:05:16,775
because it is a bank service.

73
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:20,343
So the 2,000 rent actually turned out to be more than that.

74
00:05:20,343 --> 00:05:26,291
Papa never thought that this expense should also be added to the cost of the gold.

75
00:05:26,291 --> 00:05:28,670
Truth be told, nobody thinks of it.

76
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:34,560
This expense looks small, so it stays hidden.

77
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:38,487
But it comes every year,

78
00:05:38,487 --> 00:05:43,068
whether the gold price goes up or down.

79
00:05:43,068 --> 00:05:48,303
As many years as the jewellery stays in the locker, that many years of rent.

80
00:05:48,303 --> 00:05:56,157
And along with the locker key comes the time spent going to the bank,

81
00:05:56,157 --> 00:05:58,120
line and form.

82
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:04,317
Now imagine, many years later, Mummy sells the bangle.

83
00:06:04,317 --> 00:06:11,892
She sees the gold rate, which has gone up. But the making charge,

84
00:06:11,892 --> 00:06:18,090
GST, locker rent, and the deduction when selling,

85
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:20,155
subtract all of that.

86
00:06:20,155 --> 00:06:27,730
Then you find out how much the jewellery actually earned.

87
00:06:27,730 --> 00:06:30,902
Bhai took out his phone and said,

88
00:06:30,902 --> 00:06:35,661
gold goes up every year, so what's the problem?

89
00:06:35,661 --> 00:06:39,891
Behen immediately said, it doesn't go up every year,

90
00:06:39,891 --> 00:06:43,592
sometimes it falls too. And even if the rate goes up,

91
00:06:43,592 --> 00:06:46,764
earning is a different thing.

92
00:06:46,764 --> 00:06:52,580
Earning is what is left in your hand after all the expenses.

93
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:57,808
Now the third question, where the story has a twist.

94
00:06:57,808 --> 00:07:04,998
Can there be gold that has no making charge,

95
00:07:04,998 --> 00:07:11,533
no locker, and on top of that you also get interest? Yes,

96
00:07:11,533 --> 00:07:14,801
this is called paper gold.

97
00:07:14,801 --> 00:07:21,990
That is, gold that is on paper or on a screen, not in the cupboard.

98
00:07:21,990 --> 00:07:25,721
The first form is the Sovereign Gold Bond, short name SGB.

99
00:07:25,721 --> 00:07:29,451
RBI issues it on behalf of the government.

100
00:07:29,451 --> 00:07:31,939
RBI means the country's central bank,

101
00:07:31,939 --> 00:07:36,084
which is the bank of banks too. You don't buy gold,

102
00:07:36,084 --> 00:07:39,400
you buy bonds equal to grams of gold.

103
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:45,502
The price of this bond moves along with the gold rate.

104
00:07:45,502 --> 00:07:51,050
If gold gets costlier, the bond gets costlier too. If gold gets cheaper,

105
00:07:51,050 --> 00:07:53,269
the bond gets cheaper too.

106
00:07:53,269 --> 00:07:58,817
That is, the gold risk is the same as in jewellery.

107
00:07:58,817 --> 00:08:03,810
Just no tension about making charge, locker and purity.

108
00:08:03,810 --> 00:08:08,754
Now the real twist. On top of the gold rate,

109
00:08:08,754 --> 00:08:14,316
SGB gives 2.5 percent fixed interest every year.

110
00:08:14,316 --> 00:08:19,260
This interest is paid on your initial amount,

111
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:24,204
that is, on whatever amount you bought the bond for.

112
00:08:24,204 --> 00:08:27,294
Jewellery does not give you any interest.

113
00:08:27,294 --> 00:08:31,620
It just sits in the locker.

114
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:36,492
Understand it like this. Mummy's bangles are sleeping in the locker,

115
00:08:36,492 --> 00:08:38,706
and they are asking for rent.

116
00:08:38,706 --> 00:08:41,806
The gold in the bond also sits quietly,

117
00:08:41,806 --> 00:08:45,792
but it is giving 2.5 percent interest every year.

118
00:08:45,792 --> 00:08:50,221
The gold is the same in both places. But jewellery makes you spend,

119
00:08:50,221 --> 00:08:51,550
the bond earns.

120
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:55,152
But there is a condition too, and listen to it carefully.

121
00:08:55,152 --> 00:08:57,954
This bond is meant for the long term.

122
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:01,556
Breaking a bond early through the RBI, that is, premature redemption,

123
00:09:01,556 --> 00:09:05,158
is possible only after 5 years are complete.

124
00:09:05,158 --> 00:09:08,760
And that too only on an interest payment date.

125
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:09,525
This means,

126
00:09:09,525 --> 00:09:13,735
the money you need next year for a wedding or a house,

127
00:09:13,735 --> 00:09:16,031
is not meant for SGB.

128
00:09:16,031 --> 00:09:21,389
This bond is for money you can forget about for years.

129
00:09:21,389 --> 00:09:24,451
There is also the option of selling on the stock exchange,

130
00:09:24,451 --> 00:09:27,130
but there's no guarantee you'll find the right buyer there.

131
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:30,578
And tax? This interest gets added to your income,

132
00:09:30,578 --> 00:09:34,791
and is taxed according to your slab.

133
00:09:34,791 --> 00:09:39,005
But at maturity, that is, when the bond's full term ends,

134
00:09:39,005 --> 00:09:43,219
the original buyer doesn't have to pay tax on capital gains.

135
00:09:43,219 --> 00:09:45,900
Capital gains means the profit made on selling.

136
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:52,340
Brother said, I'll buy it tomorrow itself. Sister stopped him.

137
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:56,438
New SGB issues don't come out all the time,

138
00:09:56,438 --> 00:10:00,536
first check the RBI website.

139
00:10:00,536 --> 00:10:04,048
And if you buy an old bond from the exchange,

140
00:10:04,048 --> 00:10:09,317
the tax exemption rules may be different.

141
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:12,830
Don't jump in on a tip without understanding.

142
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:19,457
The other form is gold ETF. ETF means exchange traded fund,

143
00:10:19,457 --> 00:10:26,746
which is bought and sold on the stock exchange like a share.

144
00:10:26,746 --> 00:10:32,710
Real gold is held behind every unit.

145
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:40,000
For this you need a demat account, that is, a digital account for holding shares.

146
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:44,205
In gold ETF too, there's no making charge, no locker,

147
00:10:44,205 --> 00:10:47,475
no worry about purity. And if you want to sell,

148
00:10:47,475 --> 00:10:51,212
you can sell when the market is open.

149
00:10:51,212 --> 00:10:53,081
But you get no interest,

150
00:10:53,081 --> 00:10:56,818
and a small yearly cost of the fund is deducted.

151
00:10:56,818 --> 00:11:01,490
This is called the expense ratio, that is, the fee for running the fund.

152
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:09,241
Now put everything side by side. Jewellery: the joy of wearing it,

153
00:11:09,241 --> 00:11:14,878
but making charge, GST and locker cost.

154
00:11:14,878 --> 00:11:21,220
Gold ETF: easy to sell, small fees, no interest.

155
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:26,857
SGB: you get interest, tax exemption at maturity,

156
00:11:26,857 --> 00:11:30,380
but your money is stuck for long.

157
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:36,192
Now the mistake that almost every household makes.

158
00:11:36,192 --> 00:11:40,713
We say, gold has earned so much,

159
00:11:40,713 --> 00:11:47,817
see where the price has reached. But we only count the price.

160
00:11:47,817 --> 00:11:50,400
Making charge, GST, locker,

161
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:56,858
And nobody counts the deductions when selling. Half the value lost,

162
00:11:56,858 --> 00:11:58,150
all the joy gone.

163
00:11:58,150 --> 00:12:01,334
The second mistake: treating jewellery as an emergency fund.

164
00:12:01,334 --> 00:12:04,518
Selling Mummy's bangle in hard times

165
00:12:04,518 --> 00:12:07,248
weighs heavy on the heart too.

166
00:12:07,248 --> 00:12:11,341
And then you have to sell on the jeweller's terms.

167
00:12:11,341 --> 00:12:15,435
For an emergency you need money that comes immediately,

168
00:12:15,435 --> 00:12:16,800
without any loss.

169
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:20,670
So what should we do? First, treat jewellery as jewellery.

170
00:12:20,670 --> 00:12:24,110
Buy it to wear, buy it for happiness.

171
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:27,980
Buy hallmarked jewellery, and keep the bill safe.

172
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:31,420
Making charges can be bargained too.

173
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:35,290
Before selling, ask different jewellers for their rates.

174
00:12:35,290 --> 00:12:39,751
Second, if you want gold for savings,

175
00:12:39,751 --> 00:12:43,655
then read up on paper gold.

176
00:12:43,655 --> 00:12:46,443
SGB for the long term,

177
00:12:46,443 --> 00:12:51,462
and gold ETF if you may need money soon.

178
00:12:51,462 --> 00:12:55,923
Understand the rules, tax and costs of both yourself.

179
00:12:55,923 --> 00:13:01,500
If needed, talk to your CA or adviser.

180
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:04,657
Third, don't put all your savings into gold.

181
00:13:04,657 --> 00:13:07,025
Gold is a companion in hard times,

182
00:13:07,025 --> 00:13:09,393
but its price also falls,

183
00:13:09,393 --> 00:13:12,945
and it can stay flat for years. Keep a little gold,

184
00:13:12,945 --> 00:13:16,497
and the rest in different places. This is not investment advice.

185
00:13:16,497 --> 00:13:18,470
It's just common sense.

186
00:13:18,470 --> 00:13:23,312
At the end of the story, Mummy did not sell the bangle. She said,

187
00:13:23,312 --> 00:13:26,394
this will go in my daughter's wedding.

188
00:13:26,394 --> 00:13:30,356
But the next time gold is needed for savings,

189
00:13:30,356 --> 00:13:34,318
she will sit with her sister and understand paper gold.

190
00:13:34,318 --> 00:13:37,840
Bangle for love, bond for earning.

191
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,145
Now a question for you.

192
00:13:39,145 --> 00:13:43,495
In what form is gold in your house: jewellery, coin,

193
00:13:43,495 --> 00:13:47,410
ETF or bond? Just write that word in the comments.

194
00:13:47,410 --> 00:13:49,150
And also tell me,

195
00:13:49,150 --> 00:13:54,370
has anyone in your house ever counted the locker rent?

196
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:58,919
In the next video, it's Papa's FD's turn.

197
00:13:58,919 --> 00:14:00,941
FD seems safe,

198
00:14:00,941 --> 00:14:05,490
but after inflation eats into it, how much is actually left?

199
00:14:05,490 --> 00:14:11,051
That story is also like this one, from inside the home. Until then,

200
00:14:11,051 --> 00:14:15,600
find your jewellery bill and keep it, it will come in handy.
